# Written by `bun run auth:setup` into apps/server/.env.local (ignored). Listed here for reference only.
OIDC_ISSUER=http://keycloak.orb.local:8090/realms/clew
OIDC_CLIENT_ID=clew-web
OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=
PUBLIC_URL=http://localhost:3020
# Other front ends of this installation, comma-separated bare origins under PUBLIC_URL's scheme (D67 item 6, kept by
# D88): a mutation is accepted from PUBLIC_URL or one of these, with the session's CSRF token. Clew itself has one
# front end (D88), so the list is normally empty.
FRONTEND_ORIGINS=
MASTER_KEY=
AUTH_LOCAL_HTTP=true
# Models are not configured here either: an administrator adds providers (OpenAI-compatible endpoints) and models under
# Administration › Modeller, and they live in the `model_provider` and `model` tables with sealed keys (D24). With no
# model switched on, or when it is down, the deterministic router answers (D8).
# Connectors are not configured here: an administrator registers them in the product and they live in the `connector`
# table (D23). Until the admin page exists, `bun scripts/connector-add.ts` writes the same row.
# HOST=0.0.0.0 in a container stack, so connector services can reach /api/connectors/call; loopback otherwise.
